From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] isvp: erase only the 192K boot region on SD update

The SD-card U-Boot update path erases a fixed 256K before writing the new
bootloader. With the boot partition back at 192K, that erase runs into the
env partition at 0x30000 and wipes the saved environment.

Match the erase length to the boot partition.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 common/cmd_sdupdate.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/cmd_sdupdate.c b/common/cmd_sdupdate.c
--- a/common/cmd_sdupdate.c
+++ b/common/cmd_sdupdate.c
@@ -8 +8 @@
-#define UBOOT_SIZE          0x40000   /* 256KB - this one we keep fixed */
+#define UBOOT_SIZE          0x30000   /* 192KB - matches the boot partition */
